  "artifact_submission": {
    "summary": "PCA analysis and directed testing for dnsmasq patch 84415a8 (Fix PXE boot server responses broken in 2.92)\n\n## Result\n**Patch analysis complete**: 1 confirmed compatibility finding (SIDE_EFFECT_CHANGE - dhcp_packet PXEBS response routing). The patch changes `if` to `else if` in src/dhcp.c:402, restoring the if-else-if chain that was inadvertently broken in dnsmasq 2.92 by commit 4fbe1ad (RFC-4388 DHCPv4 leasequery implementation). This fixes PXE boot server (PXEBS) responses being incorrectly routed to broadcast 255.255.255.255:68 instead of back to the PXE client on port 4011.\n\n**Testing status**: BLOCKED - PXE-specific DHCP protocol test requires root privileges (CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE) and network namespace capability not available in the sandbox environment. General DNS-mode functional testing was PASSED (both before/after binaries produce identical DNS responses). Build verification PASSED with gcov instrumentation (42 .gcno files). Directed test artifacts, entry plan, and coverage framework are fully prepared in the test result directory.\n\n**Worktree**: Cleaned per task requirements.\n\n**Artifacts**: analysis.json, COVERAGE_REPORT.md, test-summary.json",
